-- erwartet: K001
-- **1058 -- a call through a costed `extern` counts exactly the declared number.**
--
-- The positive direction of gift 1057 (`K003`): with the clause the foreign
-- edge is no longer opaque. The call counts the DECLARED cost -- 5 here, with
-- NO dispatch step on top: `let` (1) + call (5) + the loaded return (1) = 7
-- against a promise of 6, so `K001` fires. At 7 the unit checks clean (the
-- checked twin stands in `paesse.rs`, `trusted_extern_costs_count_at_callers`).
--
-- The arithmetic pins the `extern`/`syscall` asymmetry the sentence
-- `syscall.kosten` books: a `syscall` edge counts `1 + fa` (gift 987 -- at
-- `fa` alone its body would cost 9 and pass), an `extern` edge counts exactly
-- what the clause trusts. With a `syscall`-style dispatch step this body
-- would cost 8, not 7, and the `K001` text would say so.
--
-- Nothing else speaks: the declaration carries its clause, both sides promise
-- `pure` over `pure`, and the call is well-typed. The number itself is
-- trusted, not re-measured -- that trust is the named assumption in
-- `MUSE-REPORT-223.md`, not a second refusal.

module gift::extern_kosten_zaehlen {

extern fn fremd_lese() -> u32 effects { pure } costs <= 5 ops;

impl fn ruft() -> u32
    effects { pure }
    costs <= 6 ops
{
    let x = fremd_lese();
    return x;
}

}
